msgid "File locations"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"*Where EMStudio keeps its settings, recent files, vocabularies, "
"extensions and caches on each platform.*"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"EMStudio keeps two kinds of things apart. The **study** is in its em.json"
" and in the folders the study names; EMStudio writes there only when you "
"save or when a command says so. Everything else belongs to the "
"**machine**: the preferences, the arrangement of the windows, the recent "
"files, the vocabularies and extensions installed, the caches. This page "
"says where the machine's part lives."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"In the paths below, ``~`` is your home folder: ``/Users/<name>`` on "
"macOS, ``C:\\Users\\<name>`` on Windows, ``/home/<name>`` on Linux."
msgstr ""

msgid "Two places hold the machine's part:"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the **page's storage**, kept by the web view of the desktop application "
"or by the browser: preferences, arrangements, recent files, the tile "
"cache;"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"the folders of EMStudio's **local service** (the bridge, the Python "
"process that reads and writes files, runs the s3Dgraphy library and makes"
" the exports): vocabularies, extensions, plugins, the console, the caches"
" of geographic data."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the desktop both are on your computer. On the web, the page's storage "
"is in your browser, for the address of the node you opened EMStudio from,"
" and the folders of the bridge are those of the machine where the bridge "
"runs."
msgstr ""

msgid "In the page's storage"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Preferences.** Everything set in **Settings** (the six tabs), the "
"theme, the language of the interface and the experimental functions."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Workspaces and windows.** The arrangement of each workspace, the "
"workspaces you made and the names you gave them, the windows opened in a "
"separate system window, the position of panels such as the **Colours** "
"window, and the sections of the Inspector you folded."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Recent files.** The list of ``File ▸ Open Recent``: the last ten "
"em.json files opened and the rooms entered. On the desktop a recent file "
"keeps its path and opens again with a click. A file dropped into a "
"browser has no path, so on the web it is listed for memory only."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**Signing in.** The identities you signed in with (ORCID, a node) are "
"remembered here."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"**The tile cache of the 3D scene.** The tiles of a 3D tileset already "
"seen are kept on disk, in the browser's cache storage, so that a tileset "
"does not come again over the network at every return; the least used go "
"first. Its ceiling is **Tile cache on disk (MB)** in ``Settings ▸ "
"Viewers`` (1024 MB at first; 0 turns it off), with **Empty the tile "
"cache** beside it. A page opened from an insecure address has no cache "
"storage: there every tile comes from the network."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Because the page's storage belongs to an address, EMStudio opened from "
"two different nodes keeps two separate sets of preferences. Clearing the "
"browser's data for a site clears EMStudio's preferences for that site."
msgstr ""

msgid "The AI key"
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"The key of the AI service set in **Settings** is kept apart from the "
"preferences, in a place made for secrets."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"On the desktop it goes into the **system keychain** (the Keychain on "
"macOS, the Credential Manager on Windows, the Secret Service on Linux), "
"under the name ``org.extendedmatrix.emstudio``, and it is handed to the "
"bridge when the bridge starts. Settings can replace or remove it, never "
"read it back."
msgstr ""

msgid ""
"Where there is no keychain, the key lives in the memory of EMStudio's "
"bridge only, and disappears when the bridge stops."
msgstr ""

msgid "The bridge's folders"
msgstr ""

msgid "These folders are created when they are first needed."
msgstr ""

